          "source_text": "The compatibility condition is the following: pulling back the\nformal modification <MATH_0001> we obtain a formal modification\n<MATH_0002>\nSee Algebraization of Formal Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0001>.\nBy the main theorem on dilatations\n(Algebraization of Formal Spaces, Theorem\n<REF_0002>), there is a unique proper\nmorphism <MATH_0003> of algebraic spaces which is an isomorphism over\n<MATH_0004> such that <MATH_0005> is isomorphic to the\ndisplayed arrow. In other words, for some morphism\n<MATH_0006> we have a cartesian diagram\n<MATH_0007>\nof formal algebraic spaces. We will think\nof <MATH_0008> as an open subspace of <MATH_0009> without further mention.\nThe compatibility condition is that there should be a\nmorphism <MATH_0010> restricting to <MATH_0011> and <MATH_0012>\nover <MATH_0013> and <MATH_0014>.\nIn other words, such that the diagram\n<MATH_0015>\nis commutative. Observe that by Algebraization of Formal Spaces,\nLemma <REF_0003> the morphism <MATH_0016> is unique\nif it exists. We will indicate this situation by saying\n``<TEXTITOPEN_0001><MATH_0017>, <MATH_0018>, and <MATH_0019> witness the compatibility\nbetween <MATH_0020> and <MATH_0021><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>''.",
          "source_text_hash": "sha256:4d172b7743f2a89c70f0f543dfc61dba427a4c61279207deafe528f058e3bae5",
          "unit_id": "inventory:artin:0GH7:paragraph/0006"
        }
